---
import BaseLayout from "../../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetaPill from "../../../components/ui/MetaPill.astro";
import registry from "../../../data/phase-78-interjurisdictional-compacts-shared-public-value-emergency-resilience-registry.json";

const authorityMaps = registry.interjurisdictional_authority_externality_maps;
const valueCompacts = registry.shared_public_value_contribution_compacts;
const continuity = registry.mutual_aid_continuity_dispute_registers;
const emergencies = registry.emergency_authority_normalization_ledgers;
---

<BaseLayout title="Interjurisdictional Compacts And Emergency Resilience | FTFN" description="Eight inactive authority maps, eight shared-value compacts, eight continuity and dispute registers, and eight emergency-normalization ledgers.">
  <section class="page-section hero" data-compacts-registry><div class="hero__copy"><div class="eyebrow">FTFN / Shared Public Authority</div><h1 class="page-title">Coordination is not authority transfer, and emergency action is not permanent power.</h1><p class="lede">Phase 78 separates jurisdiction, treaties, externalities, public value, burdens, contributions, compact authorization, mutual aid, service continuity, disputes, emergency activation, civil safeguards, expiry, restoration, and democratic reauthorization.</p><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label="8 inactive authority maps" tone="possibility" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive value compacts" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive continuity registers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive emergency ledgers" /><MetaPill label="0 compact records" tone="review" /></div></div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Authority And Externalities</div><h2>Eight multi-authority maps remain closed.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/cooperative-federalism-municipal-authority-001/">Read the authority method</a></div><div class="grid">{authorityMaps.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.mapping_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="12 jurisdiction classes" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/compacts/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Authority, treaty, duty, standing, shared assets, cross-border flows, externalities, alternatives, conflicts, review, and receipts remain unmapped.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Shared Public Value</div><h2>Eight contribution compacts contain no terms.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/shared-public-value-allocation-001/">Read the value-allocation method</a></div><div class="grid">{valueCompacts.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.compact_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="12 contribution classes" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/compacts/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.shared_public_value_contribution_compact_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Parties, public purposes, benefits, burdens, fiscal and capacity commitments, governance, safeguards, disputes, authorization, and receipts remain empty.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Mutual Aid And Disputes</div><h2>Eight continuity registers remain inactive.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/mutual-aid-service-continuity-001/">Read the continuity method</a></div><div class="source-list">{continuity.map((record) => <article class="source-row"><div><h3><a href={'/evidence/compacts/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.mutual_aid_continuity_dispute_register_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Critical-service floors, resources, requests, command, interoperability, safeguards, priorities, disputes, remedies, handback, and closure remain inactive.</p></div><MetaPill label={record.operating_decision} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Emergency To Normalization</div><h2>Eight emergency-authority ledgers contain no activation.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/emergency-authority-normalization-001/">Read the normalization method</a></div><div class="grid">{emergencies.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><h3><a href={'/evidence/compacts/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.emergency_authority_normalization_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Threshold, lawful authority, necessity, scope, expiry, rights, oversight, continuity, evidence, challenge, restoration, accounting, and reauthorization remain inactive.</p><MetaPill label={record.emergency_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section briefing-band"><div class="briefing-band__copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public Contract</div><h2>Inspect the empty compact and emergency state.</h2><p>The export publishes authority, externality, public-value, contribution, continuity, dispute, emergency, restoration, and reauthorization controls. It contains no compact, contribution, mutual-aid activation, emergency authority, rights suspension, receipt, score, rank, or stage change.</p></div><article class="record-card"><a class="inline-link" href="/data/interjurisdictional-compacts-emergency-resilience.json">Compacts and emergency-resilience JSON</a></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
